{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C++ Header File", "description": "This file defines the interface and class for coordinating multiple runner threads within the TensorFlow training framework. Specifically, it introduces the RunnerInterface for thread execution and the Coordinator class for managing thread lifecycles, stopping conditions, and status reporting in the training process.", "external_files": ["absl/status/status.h", "xla/tsl/protobuf/error_codes.pb.h", "tensorflow/core/framework/cost_graph.pb.h", "tensorflow/core/lib/core/status.h", "tensorflow/core/platform/macros.h", "tensorflow/core/platform/mutex.h", "tensorflow/core/protobuf/config.pb.h", "tensorflow/core/protobuf/error_codes.pb.h", "tsl/platform/thread_annotations.h"], "external_methods": ["absl::Status::Status()", "absl::Status(absl::StatusCode, std::string)", "absl::Status Join()", "absl::Status ExportCostGraph(CostGraphDef*)", "bool IsRunning()", "void RequestStop()", "bool ShouldStop()", "void ReportStatus(const absl::Status&)", "absl::Status GetStatus()"], "published": ["tensorflow::RunnerInterface", "tensorflow::Coordinator"], "classes": [{"name": "RunnerInterface", "description": "Abstract interface for thread runners managed by the Coordinator, requiring implementation of Join and IsRunning methods, and an optional method for exporting cost graphs."}, {"name": "Coordinator", "description": "Class responsible for managing the lifecycle, synchronization, and status reporting of multiple thread runners in TensorFlow training."}], "methods": [{"name": "Coordinator", "description": "Default constructor for Coordinator."}, {"name": "Coordinator", "description": "Constructor that initializes the Coordinator with a list of error codes considered as clean stops."}, {"name": "~Coordinator", "description": "Destructor that calls RequestStop and Join to ensure proper cleanup."}, {"name": "RegisterRunner", "description": "Adds a thread runner to the coordinator's management, taking ownership."}, {"nam